# Project Conventions (Scholar)

## Language & Comments

- All code, variable names, function names, and comments MUST be in English
- Communicate with the user in Chinese (per user preference)
- Do not add obvious or narrating comments; only explain non-obvious intent or trade-offs
- Copyright header is required in Go files (see existing files for format)

## API Path Conventions

- User-facing API: `/api/v1/user/...` or `/api/v1/{module}/...`
- Admin API: `/api/v1/admin/...`
- All API responses use unified format: `{"code": 200, "data": ..., "message": "..."}`
- Use kebab-case for URL paths: `/api/v1/user/subscription/usage`
- Use camelCase for JSON field names in request/response bodies

## File Naming

- Go files: `snake_case.go` (e.g., `github_oauth.go`, `wechat_pay_handler.go`)
- React components: `PascalCase.js` (e.g., `MainLayout.js`, `PaperCard.js`)
- CSS files: `PascalCase.css` matching component name, or in `styles/` directory
- SQL migrations: `NNNN_description_type.sql` (e.g., `0004_iterative_fields.sql`)
- Shell scripts: `kebab-case.sh` (e.g., `run-migrations.sh`)

## Git Commit Conventions

- Use Conventional Commits format: `type(scope): description`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `style`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`
- Scope: module name (e.g., `user`, `payment`, `frontend`, `docker`)
- Description in English, concise, imperative mood
- Example: `feat(peerreview): add peer review submission endpoint`

## Security

- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or API keys
- Never log passwords, tokens, or secrets
- Always use parameterized queries (GORM handles this; never use raw string concatenation)
- JWT secrets must come from environment variables

## Error Response Standards

Backend errors follow this pattern:
- 400: Bad Request (invalid input, validation failure)
- 401: Unauthorized (missing or invalid token)
- 403: Forbidden (insufficient permissions)
- 404: Not Found
- 409: Conflict (duplicate resource)
- 500: Internal Server Error (unexpected failures)

## Testing

- Backend tests: `go test ./...` from `backend/` directory
- Frontend: component tests with React Testing Library
- Name test files: `*_test.go` (Go), `*.test.js` (React)
- Test edge cases: empty input, nil/undefined, boundary values

## Performance Awareness

- Use circuit breakers for all external API calls
- Use Redis caching for frequently accessed data (5-min TTL default)
- Use connection pooling for HTTP clients (shared instances)
- Set appropriate timeouts: reads 15s, writes 30s, streaming 5m
